# Product Requirements Document: Farm Finance Tracker

## 1. Product Overview

Farm Finance Tracker is a role-based financial tracking application for farming operations. It helps farm owners and teams record expenses, income, payments, labor costs, land rental, water usage, outsourced services, repairs, and other operational costs.

The app provides dashboard views, reports, exports, monthly email summaries, approval workflows, and audit-friendly record archiving.

## 2. Goals

- Track all farm-related expenses and income in one place.
- Support multiple farms under one admin account.
- Categorize costs such as land rental, water, labor, outsourcing, repairs, equipment, seeds, fertilizer, and transport.
- Record daily cost entries with notes, payment status, and approval status.
- View dashboards with charts and tables.
- Export reports and data to PDF, CSV, and optionally Excel.
- Send monthly financial reports by email.
- Support role-based access for Admin, Operator, and User.
- Preserve deleted records through archiving for audit purposes.

## 3. Currency

The app will support one currency only:

- Indian Rupees, INR/₹

All dashboards, forms, exports, monthly reports, and calculations must use INR.

## 4. User Roles

### 4.1 Admin

Admin has full access to the system.

Admin can:

- Add users.
- Remove users.
- Lock or unlock user access.
- Assign roles.
- View all farm data.
- Manage multiple farms.
- Add, edit, approve, reject, archive, and restore expense records.
- Add, edit, approve, reject, archive, and restore income records.
- Manage categories.
- Manage farms, fields, crops, and crop seasons.
- View dashboards and reports.
- Export reports.
- Configure monthly report recipients.
- Configure water cost rates, rental terms, and other system settings.
- View archived records.
- View audit logs.

### 4.2 Operator

Operator has limited operational access.

Operator can:

- Add daily expense entries.
- Add daily income entries if permitted.
- Update payment details.
- Upload receipts, invoices, or photos when attachments are added.
- Edit records they created, depending on admin settings.
- View operational dashboards relevant to their assigned work.

Operator restrictions:

- Cannot add or remove users.
- Cannot lock or unlock user access.
- Cannot change system settings.
- Cannot approve or reject records.
- Cannot archive or restore records unless explicitly allowed in a future setting.
- Records created by operators require approval before becoming final.

Operators do not need farm, field, or crop-level restrictions in the initial version.

### 4.3 User

User has view-only access to assigned data.

User can:

- View their specific farm, field, crop, or financial data.
- View dashboards related to their assigned access.
- View tables and reports.
- Export assigned reports and permitted data.

User restrictions:

- Cannot add records.
- Cannot edit records.
- Cannot delete or archive records.
- Cannot approve or reject records.
- Cannot manage users or settings.

## 5. Core Features

## 5.1 Dashboard

The dashboard should show a summary of farm finances using both graph and tabular views.

Dashboard metrics should include:

- Total income.
- Total expenses.
- Net profit or loss.
- Pending payments.
- Paid expenses.
- Pending approvals.
- Rejected entries.
- Monthly cost trend.
- Category-wise expense breakdown.
- Farm-wise summary.
- Field-wise summary.
- Crop season-wise profitability.
- Recent transactions.
- High-cost categories.
- Upcoming or unpaid obligations.

Graph views may include:

- Monthly income vs expense line chart.
- Expense category pie or donut chart.
- Bar chart by farm, field, crop, or season.
- Payment status chart.
- Approval status chart.
- Profit/loss trend over time.

Table views may include:

- Recent expense entries.
- Recent income entries.
- Outstanding payments.
- Pending approvals.
- Category summary.
- Monthly summary.
- Farm summary.
- Field summary.
- Crop season summary.

## 5.2 Multi-Farm Support

The app must support multiple farms under one admin account.

Farm records should include:

- Farm name.
- Location.
- Owner or responsible person.
- Active/inactive status.
- Notes.

Admin can manage all farms. Users can be assigned access to specific farm data.

## 5.3 Field Management

Each farm can contain multiple fields.

Field records should include:

- Field name.
- Farm.
- Area.
- Area unit.
- Soil type, optional.
- Irrigation source, optional.
- Notes.

## 5.4 Crop Season Tracking

The app should track crop seasons separately.

Examples:

- Wheat 2026
- Rice 2026
- Cotton Summer 2026

Crop season records should include:

- Crop name.
- Season name.
- Farm.
- Field.
- Start date.
- Expected end date.
- Actual end date.
- Status.
- Notes.

Expenses and income should be linkable to a crop season.

## 5.5 Expense Tracking

The app should support expense entries for:

- Land rental.
- Water cost.
- Water cost on hourly basis.
- Outsourced land preparation.
- Worker/labor wages.
- Repairs.
- Equipment maintenance.
- Seeds.
- Fertilizer.
- Pesticides.
- Fuel.
- Transportation.
- Harvesting.
- Storage.
- Miscellaneous costs.

Each expense entry should capture:

- Date.
- Category.
- Subcategory.
- Farm.
- Field, if applicable.
- Crop season, if applicable.
- Vendor, worker, or service provider.
- Quantity or hours, if applicable.
- Rate.
- Total amount in INR.
- Payment status.
- Approval status.
- Payment method.
- Payment date.
- Notes.
- Receipt or attachment, planned future support.
- Created by.
- Last updated by.

### 5.5.1 Water Cost

For water cost on an hourly basis, the app should capture:

- Water source.
- Number of hours used.
- Rate per hour in INR.
- Total water cost.
- Farm.
- Field.
- Crop season, if applicable.

### 5.5.2 Labor Cost

For labor and workers, the app should capture:

- Worker name or group.
- Work type.
- Number of workers.
- Hours or days worked.
- Rate per hour or day in INR.
- Total labor cost.
- Payment status.
- Approval status.

### 5.5.3 Outsourced Work

For outsourced work, the app should capture:

- Service type, such as land preparation, plowing, leveling, spraying, or harvesting.
- Contractor/vendor name.
- Work date.
- Rate.
- Total amount in INR.
- Payment details.
- Approval status.

## 5.6 Income Tracking

The app should support income entries from:

- Crop sales.
- Livestock or byproduct sales, optional future support.
- Subsidies.
- Rental income.
- Other farm-related income.

Each income entry should capture:

- Date.
- Income category.
- Crop or product.
- Crop season, if applicable.
- Quantity sold.
- Unit price in INR.
- Total income in INR.
- Buyer name.
- Payment status.
- Approval status.
- Payment method.
- Payment date.
- Notes.
- Attachment or invoice, planned future support.
- Created by.
- Last updated by.

## 5.7 Payment Tracking

The app should allow tracking payment status for both expenses and income.

Payment statuses:

- Paid.
- Unpaid.
- Partially paid.
- Overdue.
- Cancelled or voided, if needed.

Payment details should include:

- Amount paid in INR.
- Remaining amount in INR.
- Payment date.
- Payment method.
- Reference number.
- Notes.

Operators should be able to update payment details where allowed.

## 5.8 Approval Workflow

Expenses and income should support approval before becoming final.

Default flow:

1. Operator creates an expense or income entry.
2. Entry status becomes Pending Approval.
3. Admin reviews the entry.
4. Admin approves or rejects the entry.
5. Approved entries become final and appear in finalized financial reports.
6. Rejected entries remain visible for audit and correction history.

Approval statuses:

- Draft, optional.
- Pending Approval.
- Approved.
- Rejected.
- Archived.

Admin-created records may be auto-approved or follow approval settings, depending on system configuration.

Reports should clearly distinguish between approved financials and pending entries.

## 5.9 Reporting

The app should provide reports such as:

- Monthly income and expense report.
- Profit and loss report.
- Expense by category report.
- Income by crop report.
- Farm-wise financial report.
- Field-wise cost report.
- Crop season-wise profitability report.
- Worker/labor cost report.
- Water usage and water cost report.
- Outstanding payments report.
- Pending approval report.
- Vendor/contractor payment report.
- Archived records report for Admin.

Reports should support filters by:

- Date range.
- Farm.
- Field.
- Crop.
- Crop season.
- Category.
- Payment status.
- Approval status.
- User/operator.
- Vendor or worker.

## 5.10 Export And PDF Support

Users with permission should be able to export dashboard and report data.

Supported exports:

- PDF.
- CSV.
- Excel, optional.

PDF export should include:

- Report title.
- Date range.
- Summary metrics.
- Charts where applicable.
- Tabular details.
- Generated date.
- Generated by.
- Farm/company name.
- Currency as INR/₹.

Users with view-only access can export their assigned reports and permitted data.

## 5.11 Monthly Email Report

The app should send a monthly report automatically by email.

Monthly report should include:

- Total income for the month.
- Total expenses for the month.
- Net profit/loss.
- Pending approvals.
- Pending payments.
- Category-wise expense summary.
- Farm-wise summary.
- Crop season-wise summary.
- Major cost items.
- Income by crop/product.
- Comparison with previous month.
- Attached PDF report.

Admin should be able to configure:

- Report recipients.
- Report schedule.
- Report format.
- Farms included.
- Whether operators/users receive reports.

Email is the only required channel for monthly reports in the initial version. WhatsApp/SMS can be considered later.

## 5.12 Attachments

The PRD should keep attachment support as a planned feature.

Potential attachments:

- Receipts.
- Invoices.
- Photos.
- Supporting documents.

This may be added after the MVP.

## 5.13 User Management

Admin should be able to:

- Create users.
- Assign roles.
- Edit user details.
- Lock user access.
- Unlock user access.
- Remove users.
- Reset user access.
- Assign users to specific farms, fields, crops, or data scopes.

User fields:

- Name.
- Email or phone.
- Role.
- Status: active, locked, removed.
- Assigned farms/fields.
- Created date.
- Last login.

## 5.14 Access Control

The app should enforce role-based permissions.

Access should be limited by:

- Role.
- Assigned farm.
- Assigned field.
- Assigned crop or season.
- Admin configuration.

A user should only see data they are allowed to access.

## 5.15 Archive Instead Of Delete

Deleted records should be archived, not permanently removed.

Archived records should remain available for audit purposes.

When a record is archived, the system should capture:

- Record type.
- Record ID.
- Archived by.
- Archived date/time.
- Archive reason, optional.
- Original record data.
- Restore history, if restored later.

Admin should be able to view archived records and restore them if needed.

## 5.16 Audit Log

The system should track important actions.

Audit log should capture:

- User who performed action.
- Action type.
- Record affected.
- Previous value, where useful.
- New value, where useful.
- Timestamp.

Important actions:

- User created.
- User removed.
- User locked/unlocked.
- Expense added/updated/approved/rejected/archived/restored.
- Income added/updated/approved/rejected/archived/restored.
- Payment updated.
- Report exported.
- Monthly report sent.
- Settings changed.

## 5.17 Notifications

The app should support notifications for:

- Monthly report generated.
- Payment overdue.
- Pending approval.
- Entry approved.
- Entry rejected.
- User locked/unlocked.
- Large expense added.
- Report export completed.
- Failed monthly report delivery.

Notification channels:

- Email.
- In-app notification.
- SMS or WhatsApp, optional future enhancement.

## 6. Data Model

Main entities:

- User.
- Role.
- Farm.
- Field.
- Crop.
- Crop Season.
- Expense.
- Income.
- Payment.
- Category.
- Vendor/Contractor.
- Worker.
- Attachment.
- Report.
- Monthly Report Schedule.
- Audit Log.
- Archive Record.

## 7. Non-Functional Requirements

### 7.1 Security

- Role-based access control.
- Secure login.
- Password protection or OTP login.
- Admin-only user management.
- Data access restrictions by assigned scope.
- Audit trail for sensitive actions.
- Archived records must not be physically deleted by normal users.

### 7.2 Performance

- Dashboard should load quickly for normal farm data volumes.
- Reports should support large date ranges.
- Export generation should be reliable.

### 7.3 Usability

- Forms should be simple and fast for daily use.
- Operators should be able to add expenses quickly from mobile or desktop.
- Dashboard should be easy to understand.
- Filters should be clear and practical.
- INR formatting should be consistent everywhere.

### 7.4 Reliability

- Financial records should not be lost.
- Exports should generate consistently.
- Monthly reports should retry if delivery fails.
- Audit and archive records should be durable.

### 7.5 Compatibility

- Web app should work on desktop and mobile browsers.
- Mobile-friendly layouts are required for operators entering daily costs.

## 8. Suggested Screens

- Login screen.
- Dashboard.
- Farms management.
- Fields management.
- Crop seasons management.
- Expenses list.
- Add/Edit expense form.
- Income list.
- Add/Edit income form.
- Approvals queue.
- Payments view.
- Reports view.
- Export PDF preview.
- Monthly report settings.
- User management.
- Role and access management.
- Categories/settings.
- Archived records.
- Audit log.

## 9. MVP Scope

The first version should include:

- Admin, Operator, and User roles.
- Login and role-based access.
- Multi-farm support.
- Farm and field management.
- Crop season tracking.
- Expense tracking.
- Income tracking.
- Payment status tracking.
- Approval workflow for expenses and income.
- Dashboard with charts and tables.
- PDF export.
- CSV export.
- User export permissions for assigned data.
- Monthly report by email with PDF attachment.
- User management for Admin.
- Basic category setup.
- INR-only currency support.
- Archive instead of permanent delete.
- Basic audit log.

## 10. Future Enhancements

Possible future features:

- Mobile app.
- Offline data entry.
- Receipt scanning.
- Attachment uploads for receipts, invoices, and photos.
- WhatsApp monthly reports.
- SMS notifications.
- Budget planning.
- Forecasting profit/loss.
- Inventory tracking.
- Equipment tracking.
- Weather integration.
- Crop yield tracking.
- Multi-language support.
- Bank/payment integration.
- Excel export.

## 11. Open Questions

- Should admin-created entries be auto-approved by default?
- Should rejected operator entries be editable and resubmitted?
- Should crop season profitability include shared farm costs automatically or only directly assigned costs?
- Should monthly reports include only approved records or also show pending entries separately?
- Should exports include archived records for Admin-only reports?
